  "question": {
    "text": "When two tuning forks (fork 1 and fork 2) are sounded simultaneously, 4 beats per second are heard. Now, some tape is attached on the prong of the fork 2 . When the tuning forks are sounded again, 6 beats per seconds are heard. If the frequency of fork 1 is $200 \\mathrm{~Hz}$, then what was the original frequency of fork 2 ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3Hecy",
      "text": "\n$200 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Q1tXW",
      "text": "\n$202 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ri5zA",
      "text": "\n$196 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ctsNI",
      "text": "\n$204 \\mathrm{~Hz}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\left|f_1-f_2\\right|=4\n$$\nSince mass of second tuning fork increases so $f_2$ decrease and beats increase so\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& f_1>f_2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f_2=f_1-4=196\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
